{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.539185Z","id":"495f214e507aa3d9b7a795876db88517d130c4c1380943edf9ed4c1eef8e94e5","body":{"detail":"'means your person's rights changed' covers a narrowing and the owner changing the person's rights, but not a creator or the owner removing a raise of this agent (docs/contract.md 'Rights', 'Removing a raise'). The instruction that follows (leave the thread, do not ask) is right in every case. The same sentence is in plugins/clax/skills/clax/SKILL.md:430, plugins/clax-grok/skills/clax/SKILL.md:444 and plugins/pi/skills/clax/SKILL.md:424.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"a1aaba18b8dc69a136456ae53a652e4f74a85b9ed7384fa05e9a15deabeff78e"},"suggested_fix":"'means your rights on that page changed'.","summary":"The skill says a lost-access notice means the agent's person's rights changed; a removed raise or the owner's change does it too","tags":["review","task:24","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.208524Z","id":"122e3bd9b44dbd5bb2c474fafbb3c2e1acff82630077c352bddfde57921661f6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:73c2b8e3","summary":"Fixed: all four SKILL.md copies say the lost-access line 'means your rights on that page changed'. Evidence: scripts/test-plugins.sh passes (skill copies identical where required).","supersedes":"495f214e507aa3d9b7a795876db88517d130c4c1380943edf9ed4c1eef8e94e5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:02:13.694280Z","id":"c50a072c18e983bb96d47aea0b694038c552d79937462a303961c70c07572534","body":{"detail":"`Working::set` in crates/clax-core/src/working.rs, without `background`, clears the record's threads, adds the new ones and keeps the background flag only on threads still named, so a background thread left out is removed from the record and its mark disappears while its subagents still work: the defect this change exists to fix. The skill's paragraph just above (lines 383-389) tells the agent to call `working` itself when `you are acting on several threads at once`, so an owner that handed t1 off with `background: true` and is later sent t2 and t3 together, and calls `working` with `thread_ids: [t2, t3]` as told, loses t1's mark. Neither the Subagents paragraph (lines 395-407), the `thread_ids` argument description (`replaces the ones named before`, crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs and plugins/pi/src/clax.ts), the contract's Working section (docs/contract.md:4812-4817) nor the spec's list of what ends a background thread (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-06-working-across-background-subagents-design.md:86-88) mentions this. The paragraph is word for word the same in plugins/clax, plugins/clax-grok and plugins/pi's skills/clax/SKILL.md.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":383},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"da8f73ddf9f79a12717a783982f7147ed7801ce125bbf446972b5da9ee92e56f"},"suggested_fix":"In all four skills' Subagents paragraph add: `A later working call with thread_ids replaces every thread, background ones included: name the threads you handed off again (they keep their flag), or leave thread_ids out and pass only message.` Say the same in the contract's Working section and the spec's Design point 3.","summary":"The skills do not warn that a later working call with thread_ids and no background drops every background thread it does not name","tags":["review","review:pr-90","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:02:13.694320Z","id":"3b76d75fe7dc16882221fbe9cfde79c2f097cf95497cd731e7542e844cfa12be","body":{"detail":"A publish addresses only a record's foreground threads unasked (`Working::foreground_threads_of`, used by `working_threads_of` in crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs), and the paragraph forbids subagents only `working`, `comments_reply`, `comments_resolve` and `comments_handoff`, so a subagent may publish the change. The comment loop's rule (line 386-388) is to publish first so the version lists the thread as addressed before the reply; for a background thread the version lists it only if `addresses` names it, which only the `addresses` bullet (lines 155-157, `background threads aside`) implies. An owner that replies and leaves the thread open for the person's answer leaves no version listing the thread as addressed (only `comments_resolve` lists an unlisted thread, docs/contract.md:4336). Same paragraph in plugins/clax, plugins/clax-grok and plugins/pi's skills/clax/SKILL.md.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"792f377ae6b86c1dc1b0b80e87a0e7fc8ef75e99fab518e4b809c5d3647cf9fb"},"suggested_fix":"Add to the paragraph: `The publish that carries the thread's change names it in addresses (tell a subagent that publishes to do so).`","summary":"The Subagents paragraph does not say to name a handed-off thread in addresses when publishing its change","tags":["review","review:pr-90","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:05:56.696082Z","id":"9d0f714666bba531042d2681a4df3b1dbe9b304dcd1dd4d9d2d828bd4e9a256b","body":{"detail":"Working::set without background (crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:487-494) replaces r.threads and keeps r.background only for threads still named. plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md:383-385 tells the agent to call `working` itself 'when you are acting on several threads at once'; the Subagents paragraph (SKILL.md:395-406) lists the end conditions (reply, resolve, done, 10 minutes idle) without this one. `cmp` of that paragraph across plugins/claude-code, plugins/clax, plugins/clax-grok and plugins/pi skills/clax/SKILL.md finds them identical. The spec's Design point 3 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-06-working-across-background-subagents-design.md:86-88) and docs/contract.md:4812-4817 likewise omit it, though the contract's 'thread_ids and message replace the stored ones when given' implies it. Same defect as thread 636f9da5968885d984e770807a209c7ee9c6ecb4854fd3994e2d82e19e12a601 on crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:541-548; the fix belongs in whichever of code or docs that thread settles.","kind":"comment","references":"c50a072c18e983bb96d47aea0b694038c552d79937462a303961c70c07572534","span":{"start":{"line":383},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"da8f73ddf9f79a12717a783982f7147ed7801ce125bbf446972b5da9ee92e56f"},"summary":"confirmed: the skills never warn that a later working call with thread_ids drops unnamed background threads","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:05:56.696465Z","id":"e0daae87bffc952fa3aebba4a61c78c402a22978db29aa6925638c600908ebd3","body":{"detail":"A publish auto-links only foreground threads (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:591-595 -> Working::foreground_threads_of, crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:749-764). The paragraph (plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md:395-406, identical in the other three skills) forbids subagents only working, comments_reply, comments_resolve and comments_handoff, so a subagent may publish; only the addresses bullet (SKILL.md:155-157, 'background threads aside') implies the need. A reply that leaves the thread open leaves no version listing it: comments_resolve alone lists an unlisted thread (docs/contract.md:4336). Overlaps thread aeeeeb0358634ec21f0667d22ec7fb9138463cd583616fc96065b1f219be0ac0 on crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs.","kind":"comment","references":"3b76d75fe7dc16882221fbe9cfde79c2f097cf95497cd731e7542e844cfa12be","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"792f377ae6b86c1dc1b0b80e87a0e7fc8ef75e99fab518e4b809c5d3647cf9fb"},"summary":"confirmed: the Subagents paragraph does not say to name a handed-off thread in addresses","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:ee9b76d4-2000-4639-9c8f-6a12a16119a5"]}}
